{"id":"mahabharata-3-118","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":118,"title":"अष्टादशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 118 · From the south to Prabhasa","summary":{"en":"The Pandavas visit the holy places of the south, the Kaveri, the southern sea, Gokarna and Shurparaka, then travel to Prabhasa on the western coast. There the Vrishnis, led by Balarama and Krishna, come to meet them and weep to see them so worn.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರು ದಕ್ಷಿಣದ ಕಾವೇರಿ, ದಕ್ಷಿಣ ಸಮುದ್ರ, ಗೋಕರ್ಣ, ಶೂರ್ಪಾರಕ ಮೊದಲಾದ ಪುಣ್ಯಕ್ಷೇತ್ರಗಳನ್ನು ಸಂದರ್ಶಿಸಿ ಪಶ್ಚಿಮ ತೀರದ ಪ್ರಭಾಸಕ್ಕೆ ಬರುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅಲ್ಲಿ ಬಲರಾಮ ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣರ ನೇತೃತ್ವದಲ್ಲಿ ವೃಷ್ಣಿಗಳು ಬಂದು ಕೃಶರಾದ ಅವರನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಅಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"पाण्डव दक्षिण के पवित्र स्थानों, कावेरी, दक्षिणी समुद्र, गोकर्ण और शूर्पारक के दर्शन कर पश्चिमी तट पर प्रभास पहुँचते हैं। वहाँ बलराम और श्रीकृष्ण के नेतृत्व में वृष्णि उनसे मिलने आते हैं और उन्हें इतना कृश देखकर रोते हैं।","te":"పాండవులు దక్షిణ పుణ్యక్షేత్రాలైన కావేరి, దక్షిణ సముద్రం, గోకర్ణం, శూర్పారకం సందర్శించి పశ్చిమ తీరంలోని ప్రభాసానికి వస్తారు. అక్కడ బలరామ శ్రీకృష్ణుల నాయకత్వంలో వృష్ణులు వచ్చి కృశించిన వారిని చూసి ఏడుస్తారు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்கள் தெற்கின் புனிதத் தலங்களான காவேரி, தென்கடல், கோகர்ணம், ஶூர்பாரகம் ஆகியவற்றைத் தரிசித்து மேற்குக் கடற்கரையிலுள்ள ப்ரபாஸத்தை அடைகிறார்கள். அங்கு பலராமர், ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் தலைமையில் வ்ருஷ்ணிகள் வந்து மெலிந்த அவர்களைக் கண்டு அழுகிறார்கள்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ ദക്ഷിണദിക്കിലെ പുണ്യസ്ഥലങ്ങൾ സന്ദർശിക്കുന്നു: കാവേരി, ദക്ഷിണസമുദ്രം, ഗോകർണ്ണം, ശൂർപ്പാരകം; പിന്നെ പശ്ചിമതീരത്തെ പ്രഭാസത്തിലേക്ക് പോകുന്നു. ബലരാമനും കൃഷ്ണനും നയിക്കുന്ന വൃഷ്ണികൾ അവരെ കാണാനെത്തുന്നു; അവർ ഇത്രയധികം ക്ഷീണിച്ചതു കണ്ട് കണ്ണീർ വാർക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.118; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"गच्छन्स तीर्थानि महानुभावः\nपुण्यानि रम्याणि ददर्श राजा ।\nसर्वाणि विप्रैरुपशोभितानि\nक्वचित्क्वचिद्भारत सागरस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going on, the illustrious king saw holy and lovely fords, all adorned with brahmins, here and there along the sea, Bharata."}},{"n":2,"text":"स वृत्तवांस्तेषु कृताभिषेकः\nसहानुजः पार्थिवपुत्रपौत्रः ।\nसमुद्रगां पुण्यतमां प्रशस्तां\nजगाम पारिक्षित पाण्डुपुत्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bathed in them, with his younger brothers, the Pandava, son of a king and grandson of a king, went, descendant of Parikshit, to the most holy and excellent river that runs to the sea."}},{"n":3,"text":"तत्रापि चाप्लुत्य महानुभावः\nसंतर्पयामास पितॄन्सुरांश्च ।\nद्विजातिमुख्येषु धनं विसृज्य\nगोदावरीं सागरगामगच्छत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too the illustrious one bathed and satisfied his ancestors and the gods, and giving away wealth to the foremost brahmins, he went to the Godavari, which flows to the sea."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो विपाप्मा द्रविडेषु राज-\nन्समुद्रमासाद्य च लोकपुण्यम् ।\nअगस्त्यतीर्थं च पवित्रपुण्यं\nनारीतीर्थान्यथ वीरो ददर्श ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, free of sin, among the Dravidas he reached the sea that gives merit to the world, and the pure and holy Agastya ford, and the women's fords, the hero saw."}},{"n":5,"text":"तत्रार्जुनस्याग्र्यधनुर्धरस्य\nनिशम्य तत्कर्म परैरसह्यम् ।\nसंपूज्यमानः परमर्षिसंघैः\nपरां मुदं पाण्डुसुतः स लेभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he heard of Arjuna's deed, which others could not bear, he the best of archers, and honoured by great hosts of sages, the son of Pandu felt the highest joy."}},{"n":6,"text":"स तेषु तीर्थेष्वभिषिक्तगात्रः\nकृष्णासहायः सहितोऽनुजैश्च ।\nसंपूजयन्विक्रममर्जुनस्य\nरेमे महीपालपतिः पृथिव्याम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bathed at those fords, with Krishna and his younger brothers, praising Arjuna's valour, the lord of kings delighted on earth."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः सहस्राणि गवां प्रदाय\nतीर्थेषु तेष्वम्बुधरोत्तमस्य ।\nहृष्टः सह भ्रातृभिरर्जुनस्य\nसंकीर्तयामास गवां प्रदानम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at those fords of the ocean, best of the cloud-bearing, he gave thousands of cows, and glad, with his brothers, recounted the gift of cows made for Arjuna."}},{"n":8,"text":"स तानि तीर्थानि च सागरस्य\nपुण्यानि चान्यानि बहूनि राजन् ।\nक्रमेण गच्छन्परिपूर्णकामः\nशूर्पारकं पुण्यतमं ददर्श ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, going in order to those fords of the sea and many other holy places, his wishes fulfilled, he saw the most holy Shurparaka."}},{"n":9,"text":"तत्रोदधेः कंचिदतीत्य देशं\nख्यातं पृथिव्यां वनमाससाद ।\nतप्तं सुरैर्यत्र तपः पुरस्ता-\nदिष्टं तथा पुण्यतमैर्नरेन्द्रैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing some part of the sea, he reached a forest famed on earth, where the gods long ago practised austerity and the most holy kings performed sacrifices."}},{"n":10,"text":"स तत्र तामग्र्यधनुर्धरस्य\nवेदीं ददर्शायतपीनबाहुः ।\nऋचीकपुत्रस्य तपस्विसंघैः\nसमावृतां पुण्यकृदर्चनीयाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the long-armed, stout-armed king saw the altar of the foremost archer, the son of Richika, surrounded by hosts of ascetics and to be honoured by the virtuous."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो वसूनां वसुधाधिपः स\nमरुद्गणानां च तथाश्विनोश्च ।\nवैवस्वतादित्यधनेश्वराणा-\nमिन्द्रस्य विष्णोः सवितुर्विभोश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the lord of the earth saw the lovely holy shrines of the Vasus, the Maruts, the Ashvins, Vaivasvata, the Adityas, the lords of wealth, Indra, Vishnu, Savitri and the all-pervading one,"}},{"n":12,"text":"भगस्य चन्द्रस्य दिवाकरस्य\nपतेरपां साध्यगणस्य चैव ।\nधातुः पितॄणां च तथा महात्मा\nरुद्रस्य राजन्सगणस्य चैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"of Bhaga, the Moon, the Sun, the lord of the waters, the Sadhyas, the Creator, the ancestors, and the great Rudra with his hosts,"}},{"n":13,"text":"सरस्वत्याः सिद्धगणस्य चैव\nपूष्णश्च ये चाप्यमरास्तथान्ये ।\nपुण्यानि चाप्यायतनानि तेषां\nददर्श राजा सुमनोहराणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"of Sarasvati, the Siddhas, Pushan, and the other immortals, those holy and delightful places."}},{"n":14,"text":"तेषूपवासान्विविधानुपोष्य\nदत्त्वा च रत्नानि महाधनानि ।\nतीर्थेषु सर्वेषु परिप्लुताङ्गः\nपुनः स शूर्पारकमाजगाम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fasting many kinds of fasts at them, giving away costly gems, bathing at all the fords, he returned again to Shurparaka."}},{"n":15,"text":"स तेन तीर्थेन तु सागरस्य\nपुनः प्रयातः सह सोदरीयैः ।\nद्विजैः पृथिव्यां प्रथितं महद्भि-\nस्तीर्थं प्रभासं समुपाजगाम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going again by that sea ford with his brothers, he came to Prabhasa, a great ford famed on earth with its great brahmins."}},{"n":16,"text":"तत्राभिषिक्तः पृथुलोहिताक्षः\nसहानुजैर्देवगणान्पितॄंश्च ।\nसंतर्पयामास तथैव कृष्णा\nते चापि विप्राः सह लोमशेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the broad red-eyed king, bathed with his brothers, satisfied the hosts of gods and the ancestors, and so did Krishna, and those brahmins with Lomasha."}},{"n":17,"text":"स द्वादशाहं जलवायुभक्षः\nकुर्वन्क्षपाहःसु तदाभिषेकम् ।\nसमन्ततोऽग्नीनुपदीपयित्वा\nतेपे तपो धर्मभृतां वरिष्ठः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For twelve days, living on water and air, bathing in the nights and days, lighting fires all around, the best of those who uphold dharma practised austerity."}},{"n":18,"text":"तमुग्रमास्थाय तपश्चरन्तं\nशुश्राव रामश्च जनार्दनश्च ।\nतौ सर्ववृष्णिप्रवरौ ससैन्यौ\nयुधिष्ठिरं जग्मतुराजमीढम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama and Janardana heard that he was practising such fierce austerity, and those two best of the Vrishnis, with their armies, went to Yudhishthira, descendant of Ajamidha."}},{"n":19,"text":"ते वृष्णयः पाण्डुसुतान्समीक्ष्य\nभूमौ शयानान्मलदिग्धगात्रान् ।\nअनर्हतीं द्रौपदीं चापि दृष्ट्वा\nसुदुःखिताश्चुक्रुशुरार्तनादम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Vrishnis, seeing the sons of Pandu lying on the ground, their bodies smeared with dirt, and Draupadi, who did not deserve such a state, were deeply grieved and cried out in distress."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः स रामं च जनार्दनं च\nकार्ष्णिं च साम्बं च शिनेश्च पौत्रम् ।\nअन्यांश्च वृष्णीनुपगम्य पूजां\nचक्रे यथाधर्ममदीनसत्त्वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, of undaunted spirit, went to Rama, Janardana, Krishna's son Pradyumna, Samba, Shini's grandson Satyaki and the other Vrishnis, and honoured them as dharma requires."}},{"n":21,"text":"ते चापि सर्वान्प्रतिपूज्य पार्थां-\nस्तैः सत्कृताः पाण्डुसुतैस्तथैव ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं संपरिवार्य राज-\nन्नुपाविशन्देवगणा यथेन्द्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They too honoured all the sons of Pritha and were honoured by the sons of Pandu, and sat around Yudhishthira like the hosts of gods round Indra."}},{"n":22,"text":"तेषां स सर्वं चरितं परेषां\nवने च वासं परमप्रतीतः ।\nअस्त्रार्थमिन्द्रस्य गतं च पार्थं\nकृष्णे शशंसामरराजपुत्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, greatly pleased, told Krishna all that his enemies had done, their life in the forest, and how Partha, Indra's son, had gone to Indra for weapons."}},{"n":23,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु ते तस्य वचः प्रतीता-\nस्तांश्चापि दृष्ट्वा सुकृशानतीव ।\nनेत्रोद्भवं संमुमुचुर्दशार्हा\nदुःखार्तिजं वारि महानुभावाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, they were moved, and seeing the Pandavas so very thin, the Dasharhas, great-souled, shed tears born of grief and pain."}}]}]}